// Detection: Registry Run Keys Persistence
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1547.001 - Registry Run Keys / Startup Folder
// Data Source: Sysmon Event ID 13 - Registry Value Set
// Table: SysmonRegistryEvents
// Severity: High
//
// Logic:
// Detect values written under CurrentVersion\Run and CurrentVersion\RunOnce.
// Sysmon Event ID 13 stores the registry path in TargetObject and the value
// written in Details; Image is the process that made the change.
// Writes whose Details point to commonly abused user-writable folders are
// flagged with SuspiciousPath so analysts can triage them first.
//
// Tuning:
// Legitimate software (OneDrive, security agents, updaters) also writes Run
// keys. Allow-list known Image + TargetObject pairs once a baseline exists.

SysmonRegistryEvents
| where EventID == 13
| where TargetObject matches regex @"(?i)\\CurrentVersion\\Run(Once)?\\[^\\]+$"
| extend SuspiciousPath = Details matches regex @"(?i)(\\Users\\Public\\|\\ProgramData\\|\\Temp\\|\\AppData\\Roaming\\)"
| project TimeCreated, Computer, User, Image, TargetObject, Details, SuspiciousPath, ProcessId
| sort by SuspiciousPath desc, TimeCreated desc
